{
  "set": "cci-native-identifier-rows-v0.8",
  "spec": "DACS-1 §6.3.1 cci-humanpassport and cci-tlsn identifier rows",
  "tier": "candidate",
  "description": "Pins the canonical cci-humanpassport address form and the cci-tlsn claim with its web2 storage projection. Each vector models a stored node identity entry (not a ClaimReference) and the claims a producer emits when it projects that entry; only the identifier-bearing fields are modelled, and other fields a valid stored entry carries do not change the identifier. The rule predicates in tests/test_cci_native_identifier_rows_vectors.py check the vectors. The reference parser parse_claim_reference in scripts/dacs_reference.py does not yet apply the per-scheme identifier shapes, so it does not check these rows and accepts some identifiers the rows do not emit.",
  "provenance": {
    "issue": "DACS-Agent-commerce/DACS-Standard#439 and #440",
    "generator": "hand-authored normative examples; checked by the rule predicates in tests/test_cci_native_identifier_rows_vectors.py (not by a reference implementation)",
    "storageSources": [
      "node repo https://github.com/kynesyslabs/node at commit ac8f45f02fc9c25082ce9b83595c2e3916b49c5a, src/model/entities/types/IdentityTypes.ts:152-177: StoredIdentities has the keys xm, web2, pqc, ud, nomis, humanpassport, ethos and no tlsn key",
      "node repo at ac8f45f, src/model/entities/types/IdentityTypes.ts:54-56: SavedHumanPassportIdentity.address is documented as the EVM address",
      "node repo at ac8f45f, src/libs/blockchain/gcr/gcr_routines/GCRIdentityRoutines.ts:1517-1519 stores address: verification.address, and src/libs/identity/tools/humanpassport.ts:218-220 sets that value to data.address from the Human Passport API response; the node lowercases only its lookup key (humanpassport.ts:112, GCRIdentityRoutines.ts:1503), so the letter case of the stored address is not fixed by the node",
      "node repo at ac8f45f, src/libs/blockchain/gcr/gcr_routines/GCRIdentityRoutines.ts:1969-1979: a TLSN identity is pushed to accountGCR.identities.web2[context] with proofHash = Hashing.sha256(JSON.stringify(proof)) and proofType 'tlsn'; :1809-1819 limits the contexts to github, discord and telegram",
      "node repo at ac8f45f, src/libs/crypto/hashing.ts:16-20 (Hashing.sha256 returns forge md.digest().toHex()), package.json:110 (node-forge ^1.3.3); node-forge 1.4.0 lib/util.js:698-708 (ByteStringBuffer.prototype.toHex) emits lowercase hex, read from the SDK clone's node_modules, so the stored proofHash is 64 lowercase hex",
      "SDK dev-branch clone at commit 6a51c42ac6a7ea3efd2543b0469c1f1c575ef8d6, src/identity/cci.ts:413-440 (every web2 entry with a username yields a cci-web2 claim), :704-758 (parseTlsn reads web2 entries with proofType 'tlsn' and requires a 64-hex proofHash after trimming and lowercasing, :159, :721-722) and :615-666 (parseHumanPassport accepts /^0x[0-9a-fA-F]{40}$/ after trimming and lowercases it, :160, :622-624); the trim is nonBlank at :296-297, used at :622 and :721; docs/demos-cci-identities.md:15-21. Consumer-side corroboration of the projection to cci-web2 and cci-tlsn only: the node source has no cci-web2 or cci-tlsn reference"
    ]
  },
